+    <div class="content">
+      <div class="doc-category">Systems · Troubleshooting</div>
+      <h1 class="doc-title">Cannot Restart Application Engine: Post-Failure Steps</h1>
+      <p class="doc-subtitle">A stuck Application Engine process that Process Monitor refuses to restart, and the RETRYCOUNT reset that gets it moving again.</p>
+      <div class="doc-divider"></div>
+
+      <div class="doc-body">
+
+        <div class="doc-section" id="overview">
+          <div class="doc-section-title">Overview</div>
+          <p class="doc-para">When Process Scheduler or the database goes down while an Application Engine program is still running, PeopleSoft can leave that process instance in a state where Process Monitor refuses to restart it. The retry logic meant to protect against a duplicate run ends up blocking a legitimate one instead. It looks alarming the first time you hit it, but it is a short, mechanical fix once you know which two tables control it.</p>
+        </div>
+
+        <div class="doc-section" id="error">
+          <div class="doc-section-title">Error Observed</div>
+          <p class="doc-para">Attempting to restart the process from Process Monitor produces this message:</p>
+          <div class="dialog-mockup">
+            <div class="dialog-titlebar">Message</div>
+            <div class="dialog-body">
+              <span class="dialog-icon">⚠️</span>
+              <div class="dialog-text">
+                <strong>Cannot restart this request (Instance: 2319641) now. Scheduler is performing Post-Failure steps. (65,323)</strong>
+                The Process Scheduler is performing Post-Failure steps for this request, such as checking for automatic restart or execution of System Recovery Process. A request can be restarted after the scheduler completes processing it.
+              </div>
+            </div>
+            <div class="dialog-footer"><button class="dialog-ok-btn" disabled>OK</button></div>
+          </div>
+          <p class="dialog-caption">Recreated from the original Process Monitor dialog. The instance number is illustrative.</p>
+          <p class="doc-para">In practice, the scheduler never finishes that check on its own once a process is in this state. The message repeats on every restart attempt until the underlying flag is cleared manually.</p>
+        </div>
+
+        <div class="doc-section" id="cause">
+          <div class="doc-section-title">Why This Happens</div>
+          <p class="doc-para">This typically comes from shutting down Process Scheduler or the database while a process is still actively running. PeopleSoft marks the process status as No Success, but the batch server may still be working on it in the background. The instance ends up stuck between two states: reported as failed, but not yet released for a clean restart.</p>
+        </div>
+
+        <div class="doc-section" id="fix">
+          <div class="doc-section-title">The Fix</div>
+          <p class="doc-para">The restart block is controlled by <code>RETRYCOUNT</code> on the process instance, tracked in two tables: <code>PSPRCSRQST</code> and <code>PSPRCSQUE</code>. Setting it to <code>-1</code> tells the scheduler its retry logic no longer applies to that instance, and a restart from Process Monitor goes through normally. Substitute your own process instance number before running these:</p>
+          <div class="doc-code">UPDATE PSPRCSRQST SET RETRYCOUNT = '-1' WHERE PRCSINSTANCE = '2319641';
+-- Updates 1 row
+UPDATE PSPRCSQUE SET RETRYCOUNT = '-1' WHERE PRCSINSTANCE = '2319641';
+-- Updates 1 row
+COMMIT;</div>
+          <p class="doc-para">Restart the process from Process Monitor once the commit goes through. If it fails again with the same message, the update most likely did not reach the right instance number. Confirm both tables were updated and committed before trying again.</p>
+        </div>
+
+        <div class="doc-section" id="diagnostic">
+          <div class="doc-section-title">Finding Other Stuck Processes</div>
+          <p class="doc-para">A scheduler or database outage can leave more than one process in this state. This query finds every Application Engine instance sitting in a non-zero retry count that has not completed successfully, newest first:</p>
+          <div class="doc-code">SELECT * FROM PSPRCSQUE
+WHERE PRCSTYPE = 'Application Engine'
+  AND RETRYCOUNT <> 0
+  AND RUNSTATUS <> 2
+ORDER BY RUNDTTM DESC;</div>
+          <p class="doc-para">Confirm each instance is genuinely stuck, not legitimately mid-retry, before applying the same update to it.</p>
+        </div>
+
+        <div class="doc-section" id="caution">
+          <div class="doc-section-title">A Word of Caution</div>
+          <div class="doc-callout">
+            <p>Confirm restart is actually enabled on the program before forcing it back into Process Monitor's queue, and think through what re-running it will do. Some Application Engine programs send email notifications as part of their run. Restarting one that already got partway through a notification step can send duplicate emails to end users. When in doubt, check with the process owner before restarting.</p>
+          </div>
+        </div>
+
+        <div class="doc-section" id="summary">
+          <div class="doc-section-title">Summary</div>
+          <p class="doc-para">Post-Failure steps is PeopleSoft guarding against a duplicate run, not reporting a genuine application error. Once you know it is driven by <code>RETRYCOUNT</code>, the fix is two updates and a commit. The part worth slowing down for is confirming the restart is actually safe before you force it.</p>
+        </div>
